PATH RESOLUTION NOTE (no silent drift)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt's "Output" path `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Dashboard/**` does
NOT match this repository. project.yml compiles `apps/apple/Sources/**` (plus the
`apps/apple/TeslaSync/{feature-views,dashboard-widgets,shared-surfaces,...}` surface
roots), and every sibling P7 page — Powershare, SleepEfficiency, BatteryCells,
FleetCompare, the Admin pages — lives under `apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/`.
`apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Dashboard/` is NOT a compiled source root; a file placed
there would be dead, uncompiled code. So the page was implemented under the real,
build-compiled convention:

    apps/apple/Sources/Features/Dashboard/**
    apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Dashboard/**

Verified: all 8 Dashboard*.swift appear as SwiftCompile inputs in BOTH the macOS and
the iOS-Simulator builds (evidence below). Faithful interpretation of the artifact's
intent ("the Dashboard feature directory"), consistent with every predecessor P7 page —
not scope narrowing.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STRING-KEY NAMESPACING NOTE (no silent drift)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
34 of the 36 parity strings are registered in `Localization/Localizable.xcstrings`
with the web key names VERBATIM (auth.*, dashboard.*, onboarding.*, theme.firstRun*,
error.loadFailed, layout.resetMessage).

The two bare keys `title` and `subtitle` are the literal `t()` arguments INSIDE the web
page's `useTranslation('dashboard')` namespace (i.e. the fully-qualified web key is
`dashboard:title` / `dashboard:subtitle`). The flat Apple catalog has no bare single-
word page keys; EVERY sibling page namespaces its title (`sleep.title`,
`powershare.title`, `tco.title`, `statistics.title`, `glance.title`, ...). To preserve
the web namespace AND avoid a global collision in the shared 4.8 MB catalog, the two
keys are registered as:

    title    -> dashboard.title      = "Command Center"
    subtitle -> dashboard.subtitle   = "Real-time fleet intelligence and control"

Default values are ported verbatim from the web source. This is the only key-name
deviation and it is disclosed here (not silent).

