                                     ops, banner dismiss, kiosk/print/reset, derivations
  DashboardPageModel.Sample.swift    Sample (authed + unsynced -> sync onboarding) +
                                     Populated / Unauthenticated / Failing doubles
  DashboardPage.swift                View: ZStack(scroll + kiosk overlay) + header +
                                     phase switch + reset alert + templates sheet; 4 previews
  DashboardPage.Sections.swift       header + action toolbars, onboarding (GlassPanel1 +
                                     GlassPanel2 feature cards), widget board (DashboardBoardTile)
  DashboardPage.Banners.swift        banner stack: theme first-run, live-stale, customize
                                     hint, auth-not-connected, edit-mode hint
  DashboardPage.States.swift         skeleton (redacted), error region, templates sheet,
                                     kiosk overlay, redaction helper
  DashboardRouteRegistration.swift   registers .dashboard with an onNavigate seam
New (apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Dashboard/):
  DashboardPageModelTests.swift      25 XCTest cases (states/sync/edit-board/undo-redo/
                                     reset/banners/kiosk/derivations/route)
Edited:
  Sources/TeslaSyncApp.swift         +DashboardRouteRegistration.registry(base:onNavigate:)
                                     wired into routeHostRegistry (selection = $0)
  Localization/Localizable.xcstrings +44 keys (36 parity strings + 8 dashboard.widget.*
                                     board-tile titles; JSON validated, round-trip checked)
  apps/parity/apple-ledger.json      +2 rows (apple-macos + apple-ios, covered==required==41)

Note: AppRoute already declares `.dashboard` (pathSegment "dashboard", group .overview)
and `route.dashboard` already exists in the catalog, and AppRouteParser already maps the
web route "/" -> .dashboard via its "/" alias; so no AppRoute / parser edit was needed —
only the missing route-host registration.

Data sources (web parity, bound through the @Observable model; no networking in the view):
  useAuthStatus    -> GET  /auth/status      -> DashboardDataSource.loadAuthStatus()
  useSyncVehicles  -> POST /vehicles/sync    -> DashboardDataSource.syncVehicles()
  (+ supporting vehicles load -> GET /vehicles -> loadVehicles(), web useQuery(['vehicles']),
   which selects onboarding vs. the widget board exactly like the web vehicles.length check)
Web hook names preserved at the Swift call sites: useAuthStatus, useSyncVehicles.

SI discipline (ADR-005): this page renders no measured quantities — auth status (bool),
the synced fleet list (names), the onboarding copy, and the layout/board state are all
unitless. Nothing non-SI is stored or computed; no unit conversion applies here.

