PRE-EXISTING ENVIRONMENT ISOLATION (full disclosure — NOT this change; NOT red-as-green)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Two PRE-EXISTING, out-of-scope files are UNMODIFIED by this change (verified via
`git status --porcelain` — neither appears) and outside this artifact's allowed files.
A first, un-isolated `xcodebuild build` proved they are the ONLY error sources, and that
NO Dashboard file produced any diagnostic:

  1) apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/Input.Previews.swift
     2x "cannot use explicit 'return' statement in the body of result builder 'ViewBuilder'"
     (inside `#Preview` blocks) — the only `error:` lines in the clean app build.
  2) apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Admin/GDPRExportPageModelTests.swift
     "call to main actor-isolated static method ... in a synchronous nonisolated context"
     — the only `error:` line in the clean test build.

Both are the exact pre-existing failures the sibling Powershare/SleepEfficiency P7 logs
documented under this newer Xcode 26.5 / Swift 6 front-end (macOS verification is
documented PENDING in apps/macos-pending-verifications.md). They were isolated ONLY via
the command-line build setting EXCLUDED_SOURCE_FILE_NAMES (a build override — NO source
edits). With them isolated, the macOS app builds clean, the iOS-Simulator app builds
clean, and this page's 25 tests pass. Fixing those two files would breach this artifact's
allowed-files scope, so they are left untouched. Code signing was disabled
(CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO) because no development certificate exists on this runner — an
environment constraint unrelated to the page.

